  "summary": "The Alameda County Board of Supervisors voted to table a proposed extension of the Sheriff's Flock Safety ALPR contract pending answers from Sheriff Yesenia Sanchez about data sharing, ICE access, and 287(g) participation. The article also surveys recent Bay Area Flock pushback in Tiburon, Richmond, Santa Cruz, Mountain View, and Berkeley.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Board of Supervisors voted on Tuesday to table a proposed contract extension with Flock Safety",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Alameda County granted approximately 337 member agencies in the 287(g) program access to its Flock data, and they have conducted tens of thousands of searches.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Rejecting this contract today is not just the ethical choice, it's the prudent one",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
